  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What keeps pages out",
      "items": [
        "Browser tabs are sandboxed, get only the extension-API and ad-block preloads and are denied every permission but fullscreen, pointer lock and clipboard writes",
        "Every IPC channel refuses any sender but the shell view",
        "acc:// pages (documents, Cronsole runs, Git diffs, dev server logs, terminal_run run logs) run no scripts; only documents may link to documents, the rest open from the app only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What an agent can do",
      "items": [
        "Look with no click: list_tabs, read_tab, sidebar_search, recent, list_terminals, terminal_read, run_status, cron_tasks, and tab_elements, tab_screenshot on the tab the user attached",
        "Navigate: open_tab, and open_file by Hub node id (VS Code or Explorer, never the default app)",
        "Act only after Run: terminal_run starts a managed run in its own PowerShell, whose exit code is the result; cron_run asks Cronsole's run_task; tab_click and tab_fill click or type on the attached tab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who reaches the MCP server",
      "items": [
        "Claude Code in an app terminal: ACC_MCP_URL and ACC_MCP_TOKEN are in every terminal's environment",
        "The chat panel, through the same server and token, so its calls are logged and confirmed like any client's",
        "Every call, refused ones too, goes to the sidebar's MCP tab and logs/mcp.log, with the connecting client named; terminal_run's last 50 runs are searchable there too"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Optional parts",
      "items": [
        "Without Project Hub the browser and terminals still work; Files and Bookmarks offer Retry",
        "The chat needs ACC_CHAT_API_KEY and ACC_CHAT_MODEL; there is no default model",
        "Cronsole starts only when ACC_CRONSOLE_MCP names its server script",
        "Dev servers and the Git tab need a workspace folder; git and npm are found on PATH"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
